{
	"note": "Where each client parameter must land upstream, per dialect. A target names one of: path (exact dotted path), paths (any one of them), anywhere (the value appears somewhere in the body), header, or absent. 'value' overrides the expected upstream value (default: the client value); 'valueMap' translates client enum values. A path target is checked against the provider's spec: if the spec does not define the path, or its enum excludes the value, the parameter is expected to be removed (source assumed-unsupported-dropped). Dialects: openai-chat, openai-responses, anthropic-messages, gemini, gemini-interactions.",
